// n18 — `fixed` in a constant's type takes no <digits, scale>.
//
// CORBA 3.4 §7.4.1.4.2 has two fixed-point productions and a `const` takes the
// bound-less one:
//   fixed_pt_type       ::= "fixed" "<" positive_int_const "," positive_int_const ">"
//   fixed_pt_const_type ::= "fixed"
// The digits and scale of a fixed constant come from its value, so writing
// them on the type is not a redundancy the grammar tolerates — it is a
// different production, and this is not it.
//
// omniidl 4.3.4, measured 2026-08-20:
//   1: Syntax error in definition
//   1: Syntax error in abstract valuetype   (its recovery, not a second cause)
//
// The legal form is corpus/golden/30-const-type.idl. We accepted this file
// until the commit that added it, and rejected the legal one — the same
// production, wrong in both directions at once.
//
// 상수의 `fixed`는 <자릿수, 소수자리>를 받지 않는다. 값이 정하기 때문이다.
module n18 {
  const fixed<3,1> LIMIT = 9.9d;
};
